# Copy to .env. scripts/setup.sh does this.
# The API refuses to start if a value is invalid, and names it.
# Under pnpm dev the worker reads this file too, and refuses to start in the same way.

# Required for library scans. Create a free token at
# https://developer.themoviedb.org/docs/getting-started
TMDB_API_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# These have tracked defaults in .env.development and .env.production.
# Setting one here overrides both.
# NEXT_CLIENT_URL=
# PORT=
# Whether the session cookie is `Secure`. Defaults to true, and must stay true behind HTTPS.
# Browsers drop a `Secure` cookie over plain HTTP, so `pnpm dev` and docker-compose.yml set
# it to false until Caddy adds HTTPS. An old JWT_SECRET or JWT_EXPIRES_IN here is ignored.
# SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=

# Path to the SQLite file. It is created on first start. Defaults to data/app.db at the
# repository root, and the image sets /data/app.db. Keep it on a local disk, never NFS or SMB.
# DATABASE_PATH=

# Path to the media library, which must exist. Scans read it, and transcodes cache under
# it. Defaults to the media folder of this app.
# MEDIA_FOLDER=

# How many jobs the worker runs at once. Each transcode reads a whole video, so raise this
# only if your disks keep up. Defaults to 1. Under Compose, set it in a .env at the repository
# root, because the worker image has no copy of this file.
# JOB_CONCURRENCY=
